.\" nucleation(1) — mdoc, mandoc-native.
.\" Regenerate nothing: this page is the source of truth, embedded into the
.\" binary and shown by `nucleation man`.
.Dd August 4, 2026
.Dt NUCLEATION 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm nucleation
.Nd inspect, test, convert and render Minecraft schematics
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Nm
.Cm test
.Op Fl -path Ar path
.Op Fl -filter Ar substring
.Op Fl -specs Ar dir
.Op Fl -json
.Op Fl -trace-window Ar n
.Op Ar path | -
.Nm
.Cm port
.Op Fl -path Ar path
.Op Fl -specs Ar dir
.Op Fl -max-ticks Ar n
.Fl -out Ar dir
.Nm
.Cm inspect
.Op Ar file | -
.Op Fl -json
.Nm
.Cm info
.Op Ar file | -
.Op Fl -json
.Nm
.Cm convert
.Ar in | -
.Fl o Ar out | -
.Op Fl -to Ar format
.Op Fl -format-version Ar v
.Nm
.Cm diff
.Ar a | -
.Ar b
.Op Fl -preset Ar name
.Op Fl -json
.Nm
.Cm render
.Ar file | -
.Fl -pack Ar pack
.Fl o Ar out.png | -
.Op Fl -width Ar n
.Op Fl -height Ar n
.Nm
.Cm mesh
.Ar file | -
.Op Fl o Ar out.glb | -
.Op Fl -to Ar glb | usdz
.Op Fl -pack Ar pack
.Nm
.Cm man
.Op Fl -install
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is one binary over the Nucleation schematic library: a file browser,
inspector and test runner as a terminal UI, and pipeline-friendly
subcommands for scripts.
Every format the library reads is accepted by content detection, never by
extension:
.Pa .litematic , .schem , .schematic , .snbt , .nbt , .mcstructure
and friends.
.Pp
Run bare on a terminal,
.Nm
opens the shell: a browser over the current directory, an inspector per
file, and a live test screen.
Run with stdout piped, every subcommand is plain text (or raw payload
bytes), and
.Ql -
means stdin or stdout in any position that names a file, in the manner of
.Xr ffmpeg 1 :
payload bytes own stdout, status lines go to stderr.
.Sh SUBCOMMANDS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm test Op Ar paths...
Discover and run every test suite under the given paths: schematics
carrying an embedded
.Ql NucleationTest
suite, and
.Pa .snbt
structures with a
.Pa <stem>.test.json
sidecar or a
.Fl -specs
match.
Structures with no test report as unported rather than vanishing.
A single
.Ql -
reads the path list from stdin, one per line:
.Ql find . -name '*.litematic' | nucleation test - .
Exit status 1 when anything fails.
.It Cm port
Convert a corpus of
.Pa .snbt
gametest structures into self-contained
.Pa .litematic
tests under
.Fl -out ,
embedding a hand spec when one exists and otherwise synthesizing one from
the structure's own test blocks.
.It Cm inspect Ar file
The inspector: a TUI on a terminal, the text overview otherwise (or with
.Fl -json ) .
.Ql -
inspects a schematic piped to stdin (text mode).
.It Cm info Ar file
The same overview, always text:
format, size, palette, entities, machinery, and the embedded test summary.
.It Cm convert Ar in Fl o Ar out
Re-encode between formats.
The output extension picks the exporter;
.Fl -to
names it explicitly
.Pq required when writing to Ql - .
.It Cm diff Ar a Ar b
Structural diff of two builds.
One side may be
.Ql - .
.It Cm render Ar file
A PNG snapshot through the GPU pipeline
.Pq compiled with the Ql render feature .
.Fl o Ar -
streams the PNG to stdout.
.It Cm mesh Ar file
Mesh a schematic into a 3D model through the same pipeline the 3D view and
.Cm render
use
.Pq compiled with the Ql mesh or Ql render feature .
The container is
.Fl -to ,
else the output extension, else
.Pa .glb :
.Pa glb
is binary glTF for engines and viewers,
.Pa usdz
is the archive
.Xr open 1
hands to Quick Look on macOS, so
.Ql nucleation mesh build.litematic -o b.usdz && open b.usdz
is a 3D preview with nothing else installed.
Without
.Fl o
the output lands beside the input as
.Pa <stem>.glb ,
or on stdout when the input was the pipe.
The pack defaults like the GPU view:
.Ev NUCLEATION_PACK ,
else the newest installed client jar.
.It Cm man
Show this page.
With
.Fl -install ,
copy it into the first writable of
.Pa /opt/homebrew/share/man/man1 ,
.Pa /usr/local/share/man/man1 ,
.Pa ~/.local/share/man/man1
so plain
.Ql man nucleation
works.
.El
.Sh THE SHELL
Tab toggles between two kept sides: the world (browser or inspector) and
the tests screen; each side parks while the other is up, so nothing
rescans on a switch.
From the inspector, Tab runs the file being inspected; from the browser,
its directory.
.Ss Keys
.Bl -tag -width "1/2/3/4" -compact
.It Ic q
quit
.It Ic Tab
toggle world/tests
.It Ic Esc
back (collapse first where a detail is open)
.It Ic Enter
open / expand
.It Ic /
filter the browser
.It Ic i
inspect the selected test row
.It Ic r
rerun the tests screen
.It Ic 1-4
inspector tabs: overview, entities, test, 3D view
.It Ic n , p
next/previous case on the test tab
.It Ic v
cycle the image protocol on the view tab
.It Ic +/-
zoom the 3D view;
.Ic 0
resets orbit, zoom and pan
.El
.Ss Mouse
Left-drag orbits the 3D view (grab-the-model sense), right-drag pans,
the wheel zooms over the view and scrolls elsewhere; rows, tabs and the
header chips are clickable.
Dropping a file onto the terminal opens it.
Hold Shift for the terminal's native text selection while the TUI runs.
.Ss The 3D view
A software voxel raycaster needs nothing; with the
.Ql render
feature and a resource pack (or client jar) the view upgrades to the real
meshing and GPU pipeline.
Frames travel over the terminal's image protocol
.Pq Kitty, iTerm2, Sixel
with Unicode half-blocks as the universal fallback.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width NUCLEATION_TUI_PROTOCOL
.It Ev NUCLEATION_PACK
Resource pack zip or Minecraft client jar for the GPU view.
Unset, the newest installed client jar is auto-discovered (vanilla
launcher and Prism/MultiMC layouts).
.It Ev NUCLEATION_TUI_PROTOCOL
Force the image protocol:
.Ql halfblocks ,
.Ql sixel ,
.Ql kitty
or
.Ql iterm2 ,
for terminals that claim what they do not render.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
0 on success and on a fully passing test run; 1 when any test fails; 2 on
usage or I/O errors.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Convert a litematic to a Sponge schematic, in a pipeline:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
curl -s $URL | nucleation convert - --to schematic - > build.schem
.Ed
.Pp
Run every test a find(1) turns up:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
find tests/corpus -name '*.litematic' | nucleation test -
.Ed
.Pp
Inspect whatever a pipeline carries, as JSON:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
generate-build | nucleation info - --json | jq .palette
.Ed
.Pp
Render straight into an image viewer:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
nucleation render build.litematic --pack client.jar -o - | open -f -a Preview
.Ed
.Pp
Pull a build from a URL and Quick Look it in 3D
.Pq Preview cannot read glTF, so USDZ :
.Bd -literal -offset indent
curl -sL $URL | nucleation mesh - -o /tmp/b.usdz && open /tmp/b.usdz
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ffmpeg 1 ,
.Xr mandoc 1
.Sh AUTHORS
.An The Nucleation project
